      hallazgo: 'El Observador reported on 16 February 2023 that Movistar, in a fifteen-page document, called the reserved lot a "discriminatory privilege to the detriment of private operators" and asked for a closed auction; Claro asked to cut the base price from US$28 million to US$20 million, alleged an "enormous anti-competitive advantage" for Antel and demanded an eight-month deployment deadline applying equally to all operators. The GSMA warned that the base price was "high" by regional standards and that high prices discourage network investment. Ursec replied that most proposals "exceed the tender terms" and were matters for the Executive\'s decree. The outcome, according to Ámbito and Montevideo Portal, was Claro at US$28.1 million for 3300-3400 MHz and Movistar at US$28.051 million for 3700-3800 MHz, after "seven rounds without bidding". Ursec board member Pablo Siris (Frente Amplio) noted the auction "ended after 7 rounds with no bidding", and Pedro Bordaberry called it "an auction with no bids".',
